  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure remains centered over the Mid-\nAtlantic with a coastal trough off the coast. Easterly low level\nflow continues to advect moisture onshore bringing light \nshowers/sprinkles across eastern portions of the FA. High \npressure will ridge farther southward tonight allowing low \nlevel flow to veer to Nly with moisture shunted swd ending the\nthreat of light showers. \n\nHts/thicknesses build further to round out the week and temps \nclimbing back to ~10 degrees above climo with highs upr 70s to \nnear 80 inland to low 70s OBX on Friday. A reinforcing back door\ndry cool front will push through Friday night bring temps down \ncloser to climo (low 70s most locales) over the weekend. Low \ntemps will also remain above normal through much of the period \nwith readings in the 50s. Normal lows for most of the FA are in \nthe 45-50 range now. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...High pres ridge finally begins to break down by\nTuesday and esp Wednesday as next potential low pres area and\ncold front make it's way into the region on active sub tropical\njet. Still timing differences on latest 29/00Z model suite, but\nit appears this system could bring beneficial widespread rain to\nthe area. For now, due to timing differences, pops are in the\n30-40% range at this time for the mid week period.",
